\section{Profile}
\textbf{Linux} programmer and system administrator with \textbf{25+ years}
of \textbf{experience}.  Proven \textbf{track record} building
\textbf{business critial} infrastucture and services, for customers who
expect \textbf{high-availability}, \textbf{low failure rates}, and
\textbf{fast response times}.  My work also includes participation in
\textbf{open source} project (\textbf{util-linux}, \textbf{iputils},
\textbf{procps-ng}) that are installed and running on billions of devices.

\section{Highlights}
\begin{itemize}
\itemsep 0em
\item Worked on Cloudflare's authoritative DNS routing, that serves 40
      million requests per second (on average), with very low failure rate,
      and response time expecation less than 20ms per request.
\item Co-inventor, with \textit{Marwan Fayed} and \textit{Pavel Odintsov},
      on a \href{https://patents.justia.com/patent/12375442}{Cloudflare
      patent} for decoupling IP address bindings in a distributed cloud
      network.
\item DevOps team member in Lastminute.com prior the company was sold.
\item On-line web map system admin, and linux generalist for TomTom.
\item Built and ran a DNS platform serving over 20,000 domains and recursion
      for the company and customers at TeliaSonera.
\item Over 3,500 accepted open source contributions across around
      40 projects since 2009.  See OpenHub.
\end{itemize}

